P4 contract mutation (spike s008, step 9).
Change: in the 5 `valid` vectors of contract/collector-contract.json, the date folder is YYYY/MM/DD instead of YYYY-MM-DD.
The `invalid` vectors are not touched.
Tests that must fail, one per side:
  - producer: worker/test/unit/contract.test.js (objectKey still returns YYYY-MM-DD, the vector now expects YYYY/MM/DD);
  - consumer: python/tests/integration/test_pipeline.py (parse_key rejects the new valid keys).
Run both sides: the mutation is only proven if both fail.
Why not a relaxing change: if the contract accepted more keys (e.g. a `valid` vector with a lowercase `z`), objectKey would
still produce the old keys and keep passing, and only the consumer could notice; invalid keys would be accepted without
any test failing. A stricter change makes the valid data of both sides stop meeting the contract, so both suites fail.
Apply from the repo root: git apply spikes/testing-conventions/mutations/p4-contract.patch

